1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,620
Hello, this is Land Transport Information at Toronto Airport. How may I help you?

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:09,782
Oh, good morning. Um, I'm flying to Toronto Airport next week,

3
00:00:09,782 --> 00:00:14,860
and I need to get to a town called um, Milton

4
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,350
Could you tell me how I can get there?

5
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:24,312
Milton, did you say? Let me see. I think that's about 150 miles south-west of here.

6
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:29,680
In fact it's 147 miles to be exact

7
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:33,450
so it'll take you at least say, three to four hours by road.

8
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:36,030
Wow! Is it as far as that?

9
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:39,987
Yes, I'm afraid so. But you have a number of options to get you there

10
00:00:39,987 --> 00:00:43,680
and you can always rent a car right here at the airport, of course.

11
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:47,400
Right. Well, I don't really want to drive myself

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,960
so I'd like more information about public transport.

13
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:56,460
OK. In that case the quickest and most comfortable is a cab

14
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:58,493
and of course there are always plenty available.

15
00:00:58,493 --> 00:01:05,650
But it'll cost you. You can also take a Greyhound bus or there's an Airport Shuttle Service to Milton.

16
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:10,637
Hmmm, I think for that kind of distance a cab would be way beyond my budget.

17
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:15,000
But the bus sounds OK. Can you tell me how much that would cost?

18
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,880
Sure. Let's see, that would be $15 one way, or $27

19
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:26,010
50 return... that's on the Greyhound.

20
00:01:26,010 --> 00:01:31,220
Oh, that's quite cheap-great! But whereabouts does it stop in Milton?

21
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:35,808
It goes directly from the airport here to the City Centre and it's pretty fast.

22
00:01:35,808 --> 00:01:40,397
But you have to bear in mind that there is only one departure a day,

23
00:01:40,397 --> 00:01:43,150
so it depends what time your flight gets in.

24
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:48,450
Oh, of course. Hang on, we're due to get there at 11.30 am.

25
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:52,400
Hmmm, too bad, the bus leaves at 3.45

26
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:56,210
so you would have quite a wait-more than 4 hours.

27
00:01:56,210 --> 00:02:00,500
Oh, I see. Well, what about the Shuttle you mentioned?

28
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:07,261
OK. That's the Airport Shuttle that will take you from the airport right to your hotel or private address.

29
00:02:07,261 --> 00:02:11,560
It's a door-to-door service and it would suit you much better

30
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,310
because there's one every two hours.

31
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:15,000
So how much does that cost?

32
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:21,880
Let's see. Yeah, that's $35 one way, $65 return

33
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:25,050
so I guess it's a bit more expensive than the Greyhound.

34
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:29,930
Oh, that doesn't sound too bad, especially if it'll take me straight to the hotel.

35
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:32,320
But you do need to reserve a seat.

36
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,970
OK, is it possible to make a booking right now? Through you?

37
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:37,600
Sure.

38
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:43,380
OK, I just have to fill this form out for you

39
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:46,060
So what date do you want to book this for?

40
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:50,470
The 16th of October-oh, no, sorry, that's my departure date.

41
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:55,320
I arrive on the 17th, so book it for then, please.

42
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:59,040
So, that's the Toronto Airport Shuttle to Milton

43
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:02,610
And this is for just one person or...?

44
00:03:02,610 --> 00:03:04,390
Yes, just me, please.

45
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:08,492
Right. And you said your expected time of arrival was 11.30?

46
00:03:08,492 --> 00:03:13,278
So if I book your Shuttle for after 12.00- let's say, 12.30:

47
00:03:13,278 --> 00:03:17,080
that should give you plenty of time to, you know

48
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,090
collect your baggage, maybe grab a coffee?

49
00:03:19,090 --> 00:03:22,620
Yeah, that sounds fine, as long as we land on time!

50
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:27,745
Well, we'll take your flight details so you don't need to worry too much about that.

51
00:03:27,745 --> 00:03:32,550
Now, what about the fare? What sort of ticket do you want? One way or...?

52
00:03:32,550 --> 00:03:37,140
Yes, that'll be fine, provided I can book the return trip once I'm there.

53
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:42,460
NO problem-just allow a couple of days in advance to make sure you get a seat

54
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:44,110
And what's your name, please?

55
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:46,340
Janet, Janet Thomson.

56
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:48,930
Is that Thompson spelt with a 'p'?

57
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:53,180
No, it's T-H-O-M-S-O-N.

58
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:59,000
OK. And you'll be coming from the UK? What flight will you be travelling on?

59
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:05,810
Oh, it's Air Canada flight number AC936, from London Heathrow.

60
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:09,900
Right. Now, do you know where you'll be staying

61
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,030
We need to give the driver an address.

62
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:21,295
Yes, it's called the Vacation Motel, and I think it's near the town centre.

63
00:04:21,295 --> 00:04:27,710
Anyway, the address is 24, Kitchener Street. That's KITCHENER Street.

64
00:04:27,710 --> 00:04:33,320
That's fine. Right, so that's $35 to pay please

65
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,120
Have you got your credit card number there?

66
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:48,500
Yes, it's a VISA card, and the number is 3303 8450 2045 6837.

67
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:51,260
OK. Well, that seems to be everything

68
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:54,760
Have a good trip and we'll see you in Toronto next week!

69
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:57,750
Yes, bye-oh, thanks for your help!
